I've been using "vga11x19" lately.  Reasons:

- It's nice and big, coming close to the NetHack-on-console experience (but
  letting me simultaneously watch an IRC window).
- It works with IBMGraphics.  Hey, I like them :P

If you're using debian, the font can be found in the xfonts-dosemu
packages.

Here's a screenshot to give you an idea (not too much in this screenshot,
unfortunately):

http://www.cs.sfu.ca/~bclewis/personal/nethackIBM.gif

To get colours similar to the console (e.g. "bold yellow" -> brown, etc), I
have the following in .Xresources:

wterm*color0:   #000000
wterm*color1:   #cc0000
wterm*color2:   #00aa33
wterm*color3:   #cc7722
wterm*color4:   #4444ff
wterm*color5:   #cc00cc
wterm*color6:   #00cccc
wterm*color7:   #cccccc

wterm*color8:   #555555
wterm*color9:   #ff4444
wterm*color10:  #44ff44
wterm*color11:  #ffff44
wterm*color12:  #8888ff
wterm*color13:  #ff44ff
wterm*color14:  #44ffff
wterm*color15:  #ffffff

wterm*colorBD:  #ffffff
wterm*colorUL:  #ffffff

(This is obviously for a wterm.  Variables may be different for xterm, etc.)

